<h1>Natural Resources Disaster Relief Assistance Program (NRDRAP) applications Open today, Friday, August 14</h1>
<p>August 14, 2026</p>
<p>The Maine Department of Agriculture, Conservation and Forestry (DACF) is opening applications for the Natural Resources Disaster Relief Assistance Program (NRDRAP) today, Friday, August 14, 2026. </p>
<p>Maine farmers, forestry businesses, aquaculture producers, and other eligible producers who experienced weather-related losses in 2023 or 2024 may qualify for financial assistance. </p>
<p>Eligible losses may include crop loss, aquaculture loss, standing timber loss, harvested timber loss, on-farm and forestry infrastructure loss, and bare-ground practices necessary to mitigate land loss. </p>
<p><strong>Application period</strong>: August 14, 2026, through November 6, 2026. </p>
<p><a href="https://maine-dacf.wizehive.app/program/nrdrap/">Applications will be accepted through the online portal</a>. Paper applications are available upon request. </p>
<p><b>Producers can prepare now</b>. Applicants are encouraged to begin gathering documentation, including: </p>
<ul>
<li>Ownership or lease documentation </li>
<li>Parcel ID information </li>
<li>FSA Farm Number, if applicable </li>
<li>Tax or business identification information </li>
<li>Photos or records documenting damage </li>
</ul>
<p>Other records related to weather-related losses in 2023 and/or 2024 
DACF will provide technical assistance throughout the application period. Virtual office hours will be held every Friday from 11:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. beginning August 14. </p>
<p>For updates, eligibility information, and application details, visit <a href="https://maine.gov/dacf/nrdrap">maine.gov/dacf/nrdrap</a>, email <a href="mailto:NRDRA.DACF@maine.gov">NRDRA.DACF@maine.gov</a>, or call (207) 530-3144. </p>
