<h1>Public comment period opens for feedback on LSOG Forest Conservation Strategies draft document</h1>
<p>August 18, 2026</p>
<p>The Department of Agriculture, Conservation, and Forestry (DACF) has opened a public comment period on a draft document that identifies conservation strategies for late-successional and old-growth (LSOG) forests in Maine.  Maine's 132nd Legislature passed LD 1529, charging the DACF with developing a comprehensive report on statewide strategies to enhance the conservation of LSOG forests, including the management of transitioning late-successional forests. Through a work group, the DACF has engaged a broad range of perspectives to help develop the draft document.</p>
<p>Public feedback is an important step in preparing the LSOG Conservation Strategies document for the Maine legislature, as it will further broaden feedback.  DACF released a draft document for public comment on the <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dacf/mfs/policy_management/lsog-workgroup.shtml">LSOG work group website</a> on August 17: <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dacf/mfs/policy_management/documents/LSOG%20Conservation%20Strategies%20Draft_8%2014%202026%20for%20public%20comment.pdf">LSOG Conservation Strategies Draft document for public comment (PDF)</a>. An <a href="https://forms.cloud.microsoft/g/3wnRdTBLXj">online form for submitting comments</a> is also provided at the LSOG work group website. Comments will be due by August 28 at 5 PM.</p>
